WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.920
Even a casual Marvel fan will probably know&nbsp;
all about Venom, and they might know a thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.400
or two about Carnage, as well. But many&nbsp;
other alien symbiotes have appeared in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.800
comics over the years. Here's the low-down&nbsp;
on the biggest and baddest of them all.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.080
While trapped on another world, Spider-Man&nbsp;
used an alien machine in Marvel Super Heroes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:26.240
Secret Wars #8 to obtain a new, black-and-white&nbsp;
costume. After he returned to earth, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:32.240
he discovered that his new "outfit" was&nbsp;
actually a living, alien, symbiotic organism.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.440
Distraught, Peter used the loud bell tower of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.040
cathedral to divorce himself from&nbsp;
the symbiote, but in doing so, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:44.720
hand-delivered it to a man who would become&nbsp;
one of his greatest enemies: Eddie Brock.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.920
First introduced as nothing more than a&nbsp;
mysterious hand in Web of Spider-Man #16,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.800
Eddie was a newspaper reporter who was blacklisted&nbsp;
when Spider-Man debunked his claims about a local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.320
serial killer. When Peter rejected the symbiote&nbsp;
at the church tower, Eddie was praying below,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.760
and the symbiote dropped&nbsp;
down and bonded with Brock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.640
Their mutual hatred for Peter&nbsp;
united them, and they became Venom.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.760
"I like being bad. It makes me happy."

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.680
Topher Grace was the first actor to portray&nbsp;
a live-action Venom in 2007's Spider-Man 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.520
although it's safe to assume most&nbsp;
fans prefer the Tom Hardy incarnation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.520
who appeared in Venom and its sequel,&nbsp;
Let There Be Carnage. Speaking of whom…

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:34.160
When Eddie Brock and the Venom symbiote were&nbsp;
defeated and temporarily separated, Eddie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:40.800
imprisoned alongside a notorious serial killer&nbsp;
named Cletus Kasady. The two didn't exactly get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.640
along, and when the Venom symbiote finally came&nbsp;
back for Eddie, it spawned a new symbiote — one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:52.000
that bonded with Kasady at a cellular level,&nbsp;
creating the monster known as Carnage.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.800
Carnage possesses all the powers&nbsp;
of Venom, but is stronger, faster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:02.480
and more durable. Additionally, because Kasady&nbsp;
and Carnage are bonded at a cellular level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:09.440
they can’t be separated like Venom and his many&nbsp;
hosts; Kasady can simply reform Carnage at will.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.280
With his newfound powers, Carnage&nbsp;
easily escaped from prison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:18.960
and began a new killing spree. He was only&nbsp;
stopped when Venom and Spider-Man teamed up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:26.240
to defeat him in Amazing Spider-Man #362&nbsp;
and 363. Since then, Carnage has returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:31.760
time and time again to terrorize the planet.&nbsp;
Cletus Kasady made his silver screen debut in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:35.840
the first Venom movie before returning&nbsp;
as the main antagonist in the sequel.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.000
"That is a red one!"

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.040
"You need to come out right now."

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:46.480
Before 2018, Riot was one of the most obscure&nbsp;
symbiotes in the Marvel Universe. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:53.600
he didn't even get a name until Carnage, U.S.A. #2&nbsp;
in 2012, nearly a decade after he was introduced.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.600 --> 00:03:00.240
But that all changed when Sony Pictures decided&nbsp;
to use Riot as the central antagonist in Venom.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.120
"Oh God!"

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:03.600
"Where's Venom?"

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.720
"That is the ugliest looking&nbsp;
thing I have ever seen!"

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.440
Since then, Riot has become far&nbsp;
more popular with fans — although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.680
the movie did take some liberties with&nbsp;
the character's backstory. In the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:20.080
Riot is the leader of an advance party sent&nbsp;
to earth by the Klyntar species in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.360
prepare for the symbiote invasion. He bonded&nbsp;
with Carlton Drake, the head of the sinister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.320
Life Foundation, and convinced him to help&nbsp;
bring the rest of the symbiotes to Earth.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:33.920
In the comics, the Riot symbiote&nbsp;
wasn't a separate individual but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:39.600
instead another of Venom's many offspring.&nbsp;
Riot and four others were all created by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:44.640
experimenting on the Venom symbiote and&nbsp;
forcing it to reproduce five more times.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.960
Introduced in Amazing Spider-Man #298,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:54.000
the Life Foundation was created to ensure&nbsp;
the richest and most powerful people on earth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.040
could survive a nuclear war by sheltering&nbsp;
in their own personal utopia. To that end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.520
they sought out creatures that could&nbsp;
survive such a world. Enter the Klyntar.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:10.800
Collectively referred to as the "Life Foundation&nbsp;
Symbiotes," Riot, Phage, Agony, Lasher, and Scream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:16.160
were all artificially created from the original&nbsp;
Venom symbiote after it was briefly captured.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:21.680
Phage initially bonded with Carl Mach, an officer&nbsp;
of the Life Foundation's private security force.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.720
When Venom finally escaped his imprisonment, Phage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.440
and his siblings were sent to recapture him.&nbsp;
Venom subsequently teamed up with Spider-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.440
to fight the Life Foundation Symbiotes.&nbsp;
Even though they were badly outnumbered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:39.560
the duo emerged victorious using a device&nbsp;
that seemingly aged each of them to dust.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:45.280
Originally bonded with Security Officer&nbsp;
Leslie Gesneria, Agony was unique among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:50.960
her Life Foundation siblings due to her ability&nbsp;
to deconstruct and create chemical compounds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:55.200
She and her siblings all survived&nbsp;
Brock's attempt to disintegrate them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.560
largely thanks to the Life&nbsp;
Foundation's advanced technology.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.480
When the symbiotes began to gain more&nbsp;
control over their hosts' bodies, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.600
the five hosts revealed themselves to&nbsp;
Eddie Brock in the hopes that he would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.520
teach them how to stay in charge.&nbsp;
Eddie refused,believing that all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:13.760
Venom's children would eventually become&nbsp;
psychopathic murderers like Carnage.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:19.520
Agony's sibling, Scream, eventually proved&nbsp;
Eddie's fears right and began systematically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:25.120
killing off her other siblings one by one. After&nbsp;
Scream believed all of her siblings were dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:29.200
she confronted Eddie Brock — but was&nbsp;
defeated after a pretty brief fight.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:35.440
The outcast of the Life Foundation Symbiotes,&nbsp;
Scream was originally bonded with Security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:40.480
Officer Donna Diego, a woman with a history&nbsp;
of schizophrenia. After she became Scream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:45.280
she decided to test out her abilities by&nbsp;
attacking a mall in California. Spider-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.520
stopped her assault and forced Scream to&nbsp;
retreat to the Life Foundation's headquarters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:54.560
This allowed the Web-Slinger to follow her,&nbsp;
free Venom, and defeat the five symbiotes.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:58.000
Though they survived, the&nbsp;
experience sent Scream down a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.560
dark path. Suffering from her schizophrenia,&nbsp;
she attempted to kill her symbiote siblings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.360
believing they would all eventually be corrupted.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:09.840
Eventually, Donna learned to cope with her&nbsp;
mental illness and came to an understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:14.080
with her symbiote. This allowed her&nbsp;
to operate as a hero for a short time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:18.560
She helped Venom defeat a number of foes,&nbsp;
but was ultimately killed by Eddie — for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.960
the same reason she had once used to&nbsp;
justify betraying her own siblings.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:27.040
Originally merged with Security&nbsp;
Officer Ramón Hernández,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:31.840
the green symbiote known as Lasher fought&nbsp;
alongside his Life Foundation siblings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:36.400
until they were all seemingly killed at the&nbsp;
hands of Scream. Unknown to Venom, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:41.440
the United States government discovered that&nbsp;
the reports of their death were only half true.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.720
Though the hosts had all died, their symbiotes&nbsp;
had lived on, and the US government paired each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:51.760
to a different member of the elite special&nbsp;
ops military team known as "Mercury Team."

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.400
"Where do all these guys come from?"

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:58.800
Because the symbiotes were damaged from their&nbsp;
last encounter with Eddie Brock, they were each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:05.040
partially bonded to augment one specific part of&nbsp;
the hosts' body. Riot was bonded with one member's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:10.240
feet, Phage with another's hands and eyes,&nbsp;
and Agony with the last member's shoulders.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:15.360
Lasher, meanwhile, was partially bonded with both&nbsp;
the team's leader, Marcus Simms, and his German&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:20.320
Shepherd, forging a leash-like tether between&nbsp;
the pup and her master's hand. Though effective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:25.520
the symbiotes' new hosts were eventually killed&nbsp;
by Carnage during one of his many rampages.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:32.160
When Riot, Phage, Agony, and Lasher's symbiotes&nbsp;
were imprisoned within the Vault, the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:37.680
decided to violently torture and experiment&nbsp;
on them in a secret lab beneath the facility.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:42.560
Weakened by the experiments, the four symbiotes&nbsp;
merged together to survive when they were freed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:48.000
by a symbiote invasion of earth. Together,&nbsp;
this new "Hybrid" was incredibly powerful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.280
possessing each symbiote's unique abilities.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:56.480
Free from its containment unit, the symbiote&nbsp;
bonded with a prison guard named Scott Washington&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:02.080
and escaped. Though initially just as cruel&nbsp;
and indifferent as the other guards, once they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:07.920
bonded with him, Scott realized how much pain the&nbsp;
creatures had experienced. This sudden epiphany&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:13.600
of empathy changed the pair for the better,&nbsp;
creating one of the few true symbiote heroes.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.360
Ultimately, Hybrid was killed by Eddie&nbsp;
Brock when he tried to exterminate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:21.600
every symbiote on Earth. Though the&nbsp;
Hybrid itself managed to survive by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:26.240
separating into four symbiotes once&nbsp;
again, Scott himself was not so lucky.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:31.920
Cloned by the Ararat Corporation from a severed&nbsp;
piece of Venom's tongue, the symbiote that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:38.800
become known as Mania refused to permanently bond&nbsp;
with anyone, instead choosing to kill and consume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:44.560
everyone offered to it. Mania eventually escaped&nbsp;
its prison and embarked on a killing spree across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:50.320
the country until Venom could finally confront&nbsp;
and absorb the symbiote back into his biomass.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:56.320
Despite this, Mania lived on within the Venom&nbsp;
symbiote, waiting to emerge once again. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:01.680
Flash Thompson became Agent Venom for a time,&nbsp;
he used his symbiote to shield a student named&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:07.360
Andrea Benton. Much to their surprise, however,&nbsp;
that piece of symbiote bonded with the young girl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:12.480
and revealed itself as Mania. Flash&nbsp;
helped Andrea control the symbiote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:17.840
and the two worked together as heroes until&nbsp;
a criminal named Lee Price used sonic weapons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:24.480
to steal the symbiote for himself. With a new&nbsp;
host, Mania renamed himself “Maniac” and began a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:29.760
short-lived crime empire — before being defeated&nbsp;
by an alliance of heroes led by Spider-Man.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:36.080
Because they reproduce asexually, each&nbsp;
symbiote can trace its lineage directly back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:44.480
along one straight line. Venom was the 998th&nbsp;
symbiote in his line, and Carnage was the 999th.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:49.280
Venom and Carnage also knew that the&nbsp;
latter's offspring would be the 1000th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:54.240
and believed that this symbiote would be&nbsp;
more powerful than the two of them combined.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:59.760
Fearing this, Carnage attempted to kill his&nbsp;
offspring in Venom Vs. Carnage #1, but Venom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:05.520
wanted to raise the newborn as his villainous&nbsp;
ally, giving it the name "Toxin." Ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:10.640
both villains failed when Toxin bonded with a New&nbsp;
York City police officer named Patrick Mulligan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:16.240
Worried that this new host would turn Toxin into&nbsp;
a superhero, Venom and Carnage teamed up in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:21.680
attempt to kill Toxin, but were ultimately&nbsp;
beaten by the 1000th member of their line.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:27.200
Despite this victory, Patrick was constantly&nbsp;
terrified that the symbiote would take control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:32.800
and become an unstoppable monster. Because of&nbsp;
this, he fled from his family and attempted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.640
to "raise" the young symbiote as&nbsp;
a hero. His efforts were thwarted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:42.160
however, when the demon Blackheart killed&nbsp;
Mulligan and took Toxin for his own ends.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.880
Blackheart forced Toxin to bond&nbsp;
with Eddie Brock in Venom #17,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:52.400
setting the newly minted villain loose to kill&nbsp;
Flash Thompson in his Agent Venom identity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:58.240
Toxin was defeated, however, and was left&nbsp;
severely weakened as a shadow of his former self.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:02.160
During a time when Venom was&nbsp;
separated from Eddie Brock and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.760
bonded with Mac Gargan, Eddie&nbsp;
discovered that he had cancer.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.440
Eddie was eventually healed, but&nbsp;
the process completely altered the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:13.680
traces of the Venom symbiote that were&nbsp;
left within his cells. Because of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:19.360
when Venom attempted to leave Gargan and reunite&nbsp;
with Eddie, his cells rejected the symbiote.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:24.960
The portions of Venom that had touched him&nbsp;
became the new, separate Anti-Venom symbiote.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:31.120
Anti-Venom was the villain's inverse in more ways&nbsp;
than just his color scheme. The symbiote possessed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:36.400
incredible healing powers that could be used&nbsp;
to rejuvenate his host or anyone around him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:40.000
That healing ability eventually led&nbsp;
to this version's death, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.840
when it exhausted its life force to&nbsp;
heal Manhattan of a Spider Virus.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:48.640
A scientist later used remnants of Anti-Venom&nbsp;
to create a cure for Venom's toxins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.160
but when it was given to Flash Thompson&nbsp;
in a battle against Eddie Brock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:57.040
it didn't cure anything at all. Instead,&nbsp;
it turned the portion of Venom attached&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:02.320
to Flash into a new Anti-Venom symbiote,&nbsp;
allowing Flash to become "Agent Anti-Venom."

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:07.200
Before the current cosmos was&nbsp;
created, there was nothing but a void,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:13.600
and its name was "Knull." When the universe began,&nbsp;
the nearly omnipotent Celestials attacked Knull,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:19.200
and he created the first symbiote in order to&nbsp;
fight them off. Knull shaped the first symbiote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:24.320
into a blade and used it to decapitate a&nbsp;
Celestial, driving the rest of them away.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:29.120
Inspired by his success, Knull created&nbsp;
an army of symbiotes and sent them out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:37.840
to conquer the universe. When they reached&nbsp;
Earth, however, a young Thor fought them off.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.320
"Because that's what -".

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.520
"Because that's what heroes do."

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:46.320
He infected the symbiotes with a sense of&nbsp;
honor that led them to unite against Knull&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:50.880
and imprison him — seemingly forever.&nbsp;
In their language, "Klyntar" meant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:55.840
"cage," and by literally becoming Knull's&nbsp;
prison, they became the Klyntar race.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:13:01.200
Eventually, Knull corrupted Scorn — yet another&nbsp;
symbiote that originated from Carnage — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:05.600
used her to resurrect Carnage and free&nbsp;
himself from his prison. The void god&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:10.320
attempted to conquer all of existence&nbsp;
once again — but was ultimately killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:14.880
by the combined might of earth's heroes&nbsp;
… with a little help from Eddie Brock.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:19.360
